WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
I want to take a quick look at how to upload Docker Images to the Google Container Registry

00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:13.371
First, open the Google Developers Console. Then, select the project you are working on, and copy the Project ID.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:18.887
Now, we can run 'docker images' to see the list of local images on our machine.

00:00:19.068 --> 00:00:23.308
I want to push the 'go-worker' to my Google Container Registry.

00:00:23.308 --> 00:00:25.451
The first step is to tag the image.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:38.840
Type 'docker tag', then the name of the image, which is 'go-worker'. Then, type in 'gcr.io/&lt;project-id&gt;/&lt;the-name-of-the-image&gt;

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:48.780
Type 'gcloud docker push gcr.io/&lt;project-id&gt;/&lt;the-name-of-the-image&gt;'

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:53.677
Once you hit 'Enter' the image is uploaded to the Google Container Registry.

00:00:53.677 --> 00:00:56.446
This can take a few minutes depending on the image size.

